                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "49720252",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198042040932",
                            "num_reviews": 3,
                            "playtime_forever": 122,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 122,
                            "last_played": 1553366453
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played the game after the release (without success, really) and decided to try again now.  That was a mistake. I've watched dev 's \"how-to-play\" vids, I've choosen the lowest difficulty, but still I don't  know how to bit the first wave. Now it has the tutorial, but it doesn't help much. It teaches you how to move/shoot and hangs just after that.  So, dear player, no tutorial for you today. And you know what,  all your weapons just suck.  You can't blow up your enemies using the weapons, oh no. You should play strange `puzzle` game coloring your emenies in right colors just to have any chance to kill a single one. But your enemies have good old weapons which spread bullets all around the screen, so you will literely have no change to dodge them. I don't understand why the devs decided to make the game unbelivebly difficult. Is it so hard to add some newbie friendly mechanics which helps to get into the game? I don't think so. It seems the game is consciously designed as a torture, just to make sure that you will never ever run it again.",
